  abstract = {The stock market is a popular investment opportunity in the world, therefore forecasting the trends of a stock market is of significant interest to researchers. Although the highly volatile and chaotic nature of the trends makes such forecasting challenging, it can be done by considering all relevant information that affects the upward and the downward trends. Even though there are previous work performed on data obtained from well established and famous stock exchanges, such forecasting models are not guaranteed to capture the trends of stock exchanges which show high disruptive behaviours like the Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE). Further, stock exchanges such as CSE do not have trades on certain indexes on certain days making the data incomplete. In our work, we propose a forecasting model for stock exchanges with such disruptive behaviours and incomplete data. Our efforts have focused on exploiting univariate and multivariate Long Short Term Memory (LSTM) models to find the best-optimized model with the best set of features to predict stock prices and forecast the trend of indices in CSE. Going further we have built a model to find the sentiment on the economic news of the previous day which were mined from the public internet, to forecast the stock trend through text analysis. Both quantitative and text analysis models were then combined together to build the prediction model for CSE trend forecast.},
